# Competency question: "What are the first-class object kinds of the models, estimation, and
# inference vocabulary?" Exercises the STATISTICS-charter "Models and estimation" +
# "Inference and results" surface: over a worked inference scene the reasoning-free query
# reads back the asserted kind of each object — the estimation chain (estimand, estimator,
# estimate), the summary/contrast pair (statistic, statistical contrast), a model assumption,
# the process (inference run) and its plan/design apparatus (analysis plan, experimental
# design, randomization scheme), the test/sampling-distribution pair, the effect size, and the
# prediction/prediction-interval/tolerance-interval forecast objects. Scoped so items are
# fixture-local and kinds are math:. Over the fixture the answer is exactly the sixteen
# models/estimation/inference classes.
PREFIX math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/>

SELECT ?item ?kind WHERE {
    ?item a ?kind .
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?item), "http://example.org/math/"))
    FILTER(STRSTARTS(STR(?kind), "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/"))
}
ORDER BY ?item
